**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialSourcePullTests`

**How to implement.** A pulled record becomes a user material version, and updating a source re-fetches the pulled records and mints a new version only where a record changed (001 §D 'A pulled record becomes a user material version in the database, with provenance: source, record path, snapshot date or commit, licence, citation'; 'Updating a source mints a NEW version when the record changed and never mutates one'; 001 §C 'Versions are immutable'; the S13.1 brief). It REUSES the import seam's write (`CatalogueImportContext.sealEntry` and `CatalogueImportProxy.putEntryVersion`, step 94), the one path that stores a whole entry version under its own provenance and hash, as Promote to library does (step 408), and step 442's `pulledRecordsOf`, so no library verb is added. The sources live on the import context, the library-exchange seam every library window already carries (steps 101, 109, 116), so no new context is threaded. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: `CatalogueImportContext` (steps 94, 98, 104, 116, 117) gains `materialSources : MaterialSourceProxy list` (step 443), with a one-line doc: the online material sources the library pulls from, `[]` where none is composed. `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`' `create` (step 94), its signature unchanged, sets `[]`; the composition root sets the app's sources by record update (step 449), as it sets `exportFolderOpt` (step 118). (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialSourcePulls.fs`, `module MaterialSourcePulls` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `CatalogueImport.fs` and before `KitLibrary.fs` (step 139): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. It opens `MaterialLibrary`, `LibraryEntryFiles`, `MaterialSources` and `CatalogueImport`. In order: (a) `MaterialSourcePullError`, an `*Error` union: `PullSourceErr of error : MaterialSourceError`, `PullImportErr of error : CatalogueImportError` and `PullEntryErr of error : LibraryEntryError`, with `member this.describe : string` rendering `the source refused: <the error's describe>`, `the library refused the pulled version: <the error's describe>` and `the pulled material could not be built: <the error's describe>`. (b) `SourcePullChange` = `PullAddedEntry` (a new user material at version 1) | `PullMintedVersion` (the record changed: its entry's next version) | `PullFoundUnchanged` (the record's hash equals its entry's newest pulled version's; nothing written) | `PullRecordAbsent` (the snapshot no longer lists the record; nothing written), each case documented, and `SourcePullResult = { record : MaterialSourceRecordId; name : EntryName; version : LibraryVersionRef; change : SourcePullChange }`, its version the one added, minted, or left as it was. (c) `SourceRefreshInfo = { snapshot : SourceSnapshotInfo; pulls : SourcePullResult list }` and `SourceRefresh` = `SourceRefreshed of SourceRefreshInfo` | `SourceRefreshCancelled`. (d) On `type CatalogueImportContext with`: `member this.pullRecord (source : MaterialSourceProxy) (record : MaterialSourceRecordId) : Result<SourcePullResult list, MaterialSourcePullError>` reads `this.proxy.pulledRecordsOf source.sourceName` (an error is `PullImportErr`) and keeps the rows of `record`. With none, it fetches the record (`source.fetchRecord`, an error `PullSourceErr`), builds `LibraryEntryContent.ofMaterialEntry VersionNumber.first (SourcePullProvenance fetched.pull) fetched.material` (step 25) under `id = this.newEntryId ()`, as a fork takes a minted id (step 94), seals it through `this.sealEntry`, puts it through `this.proxy.putEntryVersion` with `MoveLatestVersion` (either error `PullImportErr`), and answers one `PullAddedEntry` at version 1: a user entry, because `SourcePullProvenance` is `UserManaged` (step 24). With rows, each entry they name is refreshed as (e) refreshes it, in (e)'s order, and the answer lists their results; when every entry they name is retired (e), it answers `PullImportErr (ImportRejectedErr <the record and the retired entry's GUID>)` and writes nothing, because a retired material is marked active in the Materials window, never revived by a pull. (e) `member this.refreshPulls (source : MaterialSourceProxy) : Result<SourcePullResult list, MaterialSourcePullError>` reads `pulledRecordsOf source.sourceName` and takes each entry's newest pulled row (the highest version among its rows), in ordinal order of the row's record text, then of the entry's GUID text, leaving out an entry whose held latest is `InactiveEntry` (`this.proxy.tryHeldEntry`, step 94, an error `PullImportErr`), so an update never revives a material the user retired. For each it calls `source.fetchRecord` of the row's record: `SourceRecordMissingErr` answers `PullRecordAbsent` at the row's version and writes nothing, and any other error is `PullSourceErr`. A fetched `pull.recordHash` equal to the row's answers `PullFoundUnchanged` at the row's version and writes nothing. Otherwise it reads the entry's latest envelope (`this.proxy.tryLatestEnvelope`, step 116; `None` is `PullImportErr (ImportRejectedErr <the entry's GUID>)`), decodes it (`toMaterialEntry`, step 25, an error `PullEntryErr`), keeps its id, name, category and description and takes the fetched material's `physics`, builds `ofMaterialEntry <the latest's version>.next (SourcePullProvenance fetched.pull)` of it, seals it and puts it with `MoveLatestVersion`, and answers `PullMintedVersion` at that version: every held version stays as it was (001 §C), a user's later edit included, and the record's new physics becomes the latest. The first error stops it, and the writes before it stay (step 40's rule). (f) `member this.updateSourceSnapshot (source : MaterialSourceProxy) (observer : SourceSnapshotObserver) : Result<SourceRefresh, MaterialSourcePullError>`: `source.updateSnapshot observer` (an error `PullSourceErr`); `SourceSnapshotCancelled` answers `SourceRefreshCancelled` and refreshes nothing; `SourceSnapshotUpdated info` answers `SourceRefreshed { snapshot = info; pulls = <refreshPulls source> }`. It is the job Update snapshot runs (step 450). No retry, merge, cache or option is added: a pull or an update never mutates a version (.spec-md §8). Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialSourcePullTests.fs`, `module MaterialSourcePullTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy` after its `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`, its `newEntryId` replaced by record update with a fixed test-local GUID, and step 443's double publishing the Silicon record (`main/Si/nk/Aspnes.yml`, named `Si (Silicon), Aspnes`) at `2026-11-01` under the hash of the UTF-8 bytes of `abc`, installed by one `updateSnapshot`. `a pulled record becomes a user material at version 1 under its pull provenance`: `pullRecord` answers one `PullAddedEntry` at version 1 of the fixed GUID, named `Si (Silicon), Aspnes`; `tryLatestEnvelope` of it holds `SourcePullProvenance` of the fetched pull, `UserManaged`; and `pulledRecordsOf` answers that one version. `pulling a held record again writes nothing while it is unchanged`: a second `pullRecord` answers `PullFoundUnchanged` at version 1, and the entry holds one version. `an update that leaves a record unchanged mints no version`: with `2026-11-04` published holding the same record and hash, `updateSourceSnapshot` answers `SourceRefreshed` whose snapshot is `2026-11-04` and whose one pull is `PullFoundUnchanged` at version 1, and the entry holds one version. `an update whose record changed mints version 2 and keeps version 1`: with `2026-11-04` published holding that record under the hash of `abd` and Langasite's physics, `updateSourceSnapshot` answers `PullMintedVersion` at version 2; version 2 holds Langasite's physics under Silicon's entry id and its name, with the new pull (that hash, `2026-11-04`); and `tryHeldEnvelope` of version 1 answers the envelope it answered before. `a record the snapshot no longer lists leaves its entry as it is`: with `2026-11-04` published without the record, the update answers `PullRecordAbsent` at version 1 and writes nothing. `a cancelled update refreshes nothing`: an update whose token is cancelled on its first progress answers `SourceRefreshCancelled`, and the entry holds one version. `a retired pulled material is never refreshed, and pulling its record again is refused`: after the pull, `this.proxy.retireEntry` of the entry (step 94) and `2026-11-04` published holding a changed record, `updateSourceSnapshot` answers `SourceRefreshed` with no pull, the entry holding one version, retired; and `pullRecord` of the record answers `PullImportErr (ImportRejectedErr _)` naming the record, and writes nothing. `every pull error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a wrapped test-local error renders a distinct text holding the wrapped error's `describe`.

**Acceptance.** After the pulls land, `CatalogueImportContext` MUST carry `materialSources`, `pullRecord` MUST add a pulled record as a user material at version 1 under its pull provenance, and `refreshPulls` and `updateSourceSnapshot` MUST mint the next version only where a record's hash changed, never for a retired material, and write nothing otherwise; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a pulled record becomes a user material at version 1 under its pull provenance`, `pulling a held record again writes nothing while it is unchanged`, `an update that leaves a record unchanged mints no version`, `an update whose record changed mints version 2 and keeps version 1`, `a record the snapshot no longer lists leaves its entry as it is`, `a cancelled update refreshes nothing`, `a retired pulled material is never refreshed, and pulling its record again is refused` and `every pull error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 8; kit-acceptance MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests with AT-1 and AT-2 expectations and tolerances unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s43 invariants MUST pass.
